 "result": "**Decorator:** `@needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and runs the callback inside `app.app_context()`.\n\nYou can skip it in two cases:\n- **Commands on `app.cli` or `bundle.cli`:** these already get an app context. Use `@app.cli.command()`.\n- **Commands on an `AppGroup`:** `AppGroup.command()` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`) wraps callbacks in `needs_app_scope` automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n\nThe `AppGroup` pattern is documented in `docs/cli.rst` (around line 346). Use the decorator on its own for a standalone `@click.command()`, as `shell_command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:998`) and `routes_command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:1059`) do.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`), through its `load_app()` method at line 333. `TesselGroup` (line 531) creates it and calls `load_app()` at lines 623 and 645. Inside a command you can get it with `@pass_script_info` (line 375).",
